[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m A number \( n \) has exactly three divisors if and only if it is the square of a prime number. This is because the divisors of \( p^2 \) (where \( p \) is a prime) are \( 1, p, \) and \( p^2 \). Any other form of number will either have fewer or more than three divisors.
