[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m    The incenter \( I \) is the point where the angle bisectors of the triangle meet. In an isosceles triangle, the angle bisector of the vertex angle is also the altitude and median. Therefore, \( AD \) is the angle bisector of \( \angle BAC \), and it passes through the incenter \( I \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
