[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 3. **Number of years**: We are considering a period of 10 years.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 4. **Total increase in trees over 10 years**: Over 10 years, the total increase in the number of trees is \(8 \times 10 = 80\) trees.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 5. **Total number of trees after 10 years before any die**: Adding the initial number of trees to the total increase, we get \(50 + 80 = 130\) trees.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 6. **Percentage of trees that die**: After 10 years, 30% of the trees die. So, the number of trees that die is \(0.30 \times 130 = 39\) trees.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 7. **Number of trees left after 30% die**: Subtracting the number of trees that die from the total number of trees after 10 years, we get \(130 - 39 = 91\) trees.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m #### 91
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m So, after following the steps, the answer is 91.
