[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m - \( a = 4 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m - \( b = 7 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m - \( c = k \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The roots of the equation are given as \( \frac{-7 \pm i\sqrt{15}}{8} \). We can compare this with the quadratic formula to find the value of \( k \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m First, let's identify the discriminant from the given roots. The discriminant \( \Delta \) of a quadratic equation \( ax^2 + bx + c = 0 \) is given by:
