[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Next, we need to find the LCM of \(\frac{3}{100}\) and \(\frac{1}{45}\). To do this, we first find the LCM of the numerators (3 and 1) and the GCD (greatest common divisor) of the denominators (100 and 45).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
