[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m **Step 1: Calculate the cost per sneaker.**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The salesman bought 48 sneakers for $576. So, the cost per sneaker is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[ \text{Cost per sneaker} = \frac{\$576}{48} = \$12 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m **Step 2: Calculate the total revenue from selling the sneakers.**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m - He sold 17 sneakers for $20 each at a flash sale on Monday, so the revenue from Monday is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[ 17 \times \$20 = \$340 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m - The rest of the sneakers (48 - 17 = 31 sneakers) were sold to a department store for $25 each, so the revenue from the department store is:
