[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 1. **Determine the expected value of a single die roll:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m    - An eight-sided die has faces numbered from 1 to 8.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m    - The expected value \(E(X)\) of a single roll of an eight-sided die is the average of all possible outcomes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m    - The formula for the expected value of a discrete uniform distribution is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m      E(X) = \frac{1 + 2 + 3 + \cdots + 8}{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m    - The sum of the first \(n\) positive integers is given by the formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m      \sum_{i=1}^{n} i = \frac{n(n+1)}{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m    - For \(n = 8\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m      \sum_{i=1}^{8} i = \frac{8 \cdot 9}{2} = 36
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m    - Therefore, the expected value of a single die roll is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m      E(X) = \frac{36}{8} = 4.5
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 2. **Determine the expected value of the sum of two dice rolls:**
