[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m A natural number \( n \) has exactly three distinct positive integer divisors if and only if it is the square of a prime number. This is because the divisors of \( n = p^2 \) (where \( p \) is a prime number) are \( 1, p, \) and \( p^2 \). Any other form of \( n \) would either have fewer or more than three divisors.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Let's list the squares of prime numbers that are less than 1000:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
