[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Using the formula \(F = ma\), we can write:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[ m_s \cdot a_s = m_b \cdot a_b \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Where \(a_s\) is the acceleration of the softball and \(a_b\) is the acceleration of the baseball. We need to find the ratio of the acceleration of Jen's ball to Jack's ball, which is \(\frac{a_s}{a_b}\).
