[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The formula for the height of the plant after \( n \) days, given an initial height \( H_0 \) and a daily growth rate of \( r \), is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[ H = H_0 \times (1 + r)^n \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Here, \( H = 452 \) cm, \( r = 0.05 \), and \( n = 14 \). We need to find \( H_0 \), the height of the plant 14 days ago. Rearranging the formula to solve for \( H_0 \), we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[ H_0 = \frac{H}{(1 + r)^n} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
