[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Starting with the expression \(x^2 - 6x + 13\), we focus on the first two terms, \(x^2 - 6x\). To complete the square, we take half of the coefficient of \(x\), which is \(-6\), divide it by 2 to get \(-3\), and then square it to get \(9\). We add and subtract this square inside the expression:
