[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m [response] To find the future value of Paula's investment, we use the formula for compound interest:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[ A = P \left(1 + \frac{r}{n}\right)^{nt} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m where:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m - \( A \) is the amount of money accumulated after \( n \) years, including interest.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m - \( P \) is the principal amount (the initial amount of money).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m - \( r \) is the annual interest rate (decimal).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m - \( n \) is the number of times that interest is compounded per year.
