[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The triangle inequality theorem gives us the following conditions:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 1. \(8 + 8 > x\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 2. \(8 + x > 8\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 3. \(8 + x > 8\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Simplifying these inequalities, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 1. \(16 > x\) or \(x < 16\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 2. \(x > 0\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 3. \(x > 0\)
