[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m    - Let the isosceles triangle be \( \triangle ABC \) with \( AB = AC \) and \( BC = a \), \( AB = AC = b \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m    - The vertex angle is \( \angle BAC = \theta \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m    - The base angles are \( \angle ABC = \angle ACB = \frac{180^\circ - \theta}{2} \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 2. **Understand the intersection of altitudes and the incircle:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m    - The altitudes of an isosceles triangle intersect at the orthocenter.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m    - The condition that the altitudes intersect on the incircle implies that the orthocenter lies on the incircle. This is a special case that occurs when the triangle is a right isosceles triangle or when the vertex angle is \( 120^\circ \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 3. **Determine the vertex angle:**
