[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The roots of a quadratic equation $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$ are given by the quadratic formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Comparing this with the given roots $\frac{-7\pm i\sqrt{15}}{8}$, we can see that $a = 4$, $b = 7$, and the discriminant $b^2 - 4ac$ must be $-15$ (since the roots are complex and the imaginary part is $\sqrt{15}$).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The discriminant of the quadratic equation is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[b^2 - 4ac = 7^2 - 4(4)k = 49 - 16k\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
