[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The population of Rod doubles every hour, so the population of Rod at time \( t \) is \( 2 \times 2^t = 2^{t+1} \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The population of Sphere quadruples every hour, so the population of Sphere at time \( t - 5 \) is \( 8 \times 4^{t-5} = 8 \times (2^2)^{t-5} = 8 \times 2^{2(t-5)} = 2^3 \times 2^{2t-10} = 2^{2t-7} \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m At 8 p.m., the populations of both farms are the same, so we can set the two expressions equal to each other:
