[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m [response] Let's denote the number of hours since Jane started growing Rod as \(t\). Since she started growing Sphere 5 hours later, the time since she started growing Sphere is \(t-5\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The population of Rod at time \(t\) is \(2 \times 2^t = 2^{t+1}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The population of Sphere at time \(t-5\) is \(8 \times 4^{t-5} = 2^3 \times (2^2)^{t-5} = 2^{2t-7}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Since the populations are equal at 8 p.m., we have:
