[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m [response] To find the speed of the particle, we first need to find the velocity vector of the particle. The position of the particle at time $t$ is given by $\left( 3 \sin \frac{t}{4}, 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \right)$. The velocity vector is the derivative of the position vector with respect to time $t$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The velocity vector is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \left( \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \sin \frac{t}{4} \right), \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \right) \right) = \left( \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4}, -\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4} \right)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
