[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m [response] Given the quadratic equation $4x^2 + 7x + k$ with roots $\frac{-7\pm i\sqrt{15}}{8}$, we can use the fact that the sum and product of the roots of a quadratic equation $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$ are given by $-\frac{b}{a}$ and $\frac{c}{a}$, respectively.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
