[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The $x$-component of the position is $3 \sin \frac{t}{4}$, and the $y$-component is $3 \cos \frac{t}{4}$. Differentiating these with respect to $t$ gives us the velocity components:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m v_x = \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \sin \frac{t}{4} \right) = \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[
