[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m [response] Given that the distance from the starting point to the last house is $\sqrt{2012}$ on both days, we can use the fact that the distance between two points in the complex plane is the modulus of their difference. On Saturday, Eli travels from $z$ to $z^{2013}$, and on Sunday, from $1$ to $z^{2012}$. Therefore, we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[|z^{2013} - z| = \sqrt{2012}\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[|z^{2012} - 1| = \sqrt{2012}\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Since $|z^{2013} - z| = |z||z^{2012} - 1|$, we can infer that $|z| = 1$. This means $z$ lies on the unit circle, and we can write $z = e^{i\theta}$ for some angle $\theta$. Then $z^2 = e^{2i\theta}$, and we need to find the real part of $z^2$, which is $\cos(2\theta)$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Since $|z^{2012} - 1| = \sqrt{2012}$, we can write $z^{2012} = e^{2012i\theta} = -1$ (since the distance from $1$ to $-1$ is $\sqrt{2012}$, and $2012\theta$ must be an odd multiple of $\pi$). This means $2012\theta = (2k+1)\pi$ for some integer $k$, and $\theta = \frac{(2k+1)\pi}{2012}$. Therefore, $2\theta = \frac{(2k+1)\pi}{1006}$, and $\cos(2\theta) = \cos\left(\frac{(2k+1)\pi}{1006}\right) = -1$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Thus, the real part of $z^2$ is $\boxed{-1}$.
