[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m [response] Given the problem, we know that the distance from the starting point to the last house is $\sqrt{2012}$ on both days. On Saturday, Eli starts at $z$ and ends at $z^{2013}$, and on Sunday, he starts at $1$ and ends at $z^{2012}$. The distance from $z$ to $z^{2013}$ and from $1$ to $z^{2012}$ is $\sqrt{2012}$. This implies that $|z^{2012} - 1| = \sqrt{2012}$ and $|z^{2013} - z| = \sqrt{2012}$. Since $|z^{2013} - z| = |z||z^{2012} - 1|$, we have $|z| = 1$. Therefore, $z$ lies on the unit circle, and $z = e^{i\theta}$ for some $\theta$. We have $|e^{2012i\theta} - 1| = \sqrt{2012}$. This means $2012\theta = \pi + 2k\pi$ for some integer $k$, so $\theta = \frac{\pi(2k+1)}{2012}$. The real part of $z^2 = e^{2i\theta}$ is $\cos(2\theta) = \cos\left(\frac{\pi(2k+1)}{1006}\right)$. For $k=0$, we get $\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{1006}\right)$. The real part of $z^2$ is \boxed{-1}.
