[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m [response] First, we square both sides of the equation to get rid of the square roots:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[5|x| + 8 = x^2 - 16.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[x^2 - 5|x| - 24 = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m We consider two cases: \(x \geq 0\) and \(x < 0\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m For \(x \geq 0\), the equation becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[x^2 - 5x - 24 = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Factoring, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[(x - 8)(x + 3) = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Thus, \(x = 8\) or \(x = -3\), but since \(x \geq 0\), we only take \(x = 8\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m For \(x < 0\), the equation becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[x^2 + 5x - 24 = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Factoring, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[(x + 8)(x - 3) = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Thus, \(x = -8\) or \(x = 3\), but since \(x < 0\), we only take \(x = -8\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
