[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m To find the time when both gears will have their marks pointing due north again, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of the periods of the two gears. The period of the first gear is \(\frac{3}{100}\) minutes per rotation, and the period of the second gear is \(\frac{1}{45}\) minutes per rotation.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
