[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m [response] To solve this, we need to calculate the volume of the cylindrical beaker and the volume of the spherical tank, and then determine how many beakers are needed to fill the tank.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The volume of a cylinder is given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[ V_{\text{cylinder}} = \pi r^2 h \]
