[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m [response] The position of the particle at time $t$ is given by $\left( 3 \sin \frac{t}{4}, 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \right)$. To find the speed, we first need to determine the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector with respect to time $t$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The $x$-coordinate is $3 \sin \frac{t}{4}$, and the $y$-coordinate is $3 \cos \frac{t}{4}$. Differentiating these with respect to $t$ gives us the velocity components:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \frac{dx}{dt} = \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4}, \quad \frac{dy}{dt} = -\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4}.
