[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m [response] Given the quadratic equation $4x^2 + 7x + k$ with roots $\frac{-7\pm i\sqrt{15}}{8}$, we can use the fact that for a quadratic equation $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$, the sum and product of the roots are given by $-b/a$ and $c/a$, respectively.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
