[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m &\equiv -13 \pmod{99} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m &\equiv 86 \pmod{99} && \text{(since $-13 + 99 = 86$)}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m We are to find $n$ in $\{1000, 1001, \ldots, 1098\}$ such that $n \equiv 86 \pmod{99}$. We express $n$ as $99k + 86$ for some integer $k$ and find $k$ such that $n$ is in the given range:
