[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Differentiating each component with respect to $t$ gives us the velocity vector:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m x'(t) &= \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \sin \frac{t}{4} \right) = \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4}, \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m y'(t) &= \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \right) = -\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m The speed of the particle is the magnitude of the velocity vector:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \begin{align*}
