[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we first need to understand the behavior of the functions $f$ and $g$ when applied successively. Let's start by computing the first few iterations of the functions applied to an arbitrary $x$ and then specifically to $12$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m First, we compute $f(g(x))$:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m g(x) &= \frac{-2}{x+1} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m f(g(x)) &= f\left(\frac{-2}{x+1}\right) = \frac{1 + \frac{-2}{x+1}}{1 - \frac{-2}{x+1}} = \frac{\frac{x+1-2}{x+1}}{\frac{x+1+2}{x+1}} = \frac{x-1}{x+3}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m Next, we compute $g(f(x))$:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m f(x) &= \frac{1+x}{1-x} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m g(f(x)) &= g\left(\frac{1+x}{1-x}\right) = \frac{-2}{\frac{1+x}{1-x} + 1} = \frac{-2}{\frac{1+x+1-x}{1-x}} = \frac{-2(1-x)}{2} = x-1.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1536333)[0m We notice that $g(f(x)) = x - 1$. This is a key observation. Now, we apply this to our problem. We start with $12$ and apply $f$ and $g$ alternately 8 times each. Since $g(f(x)) = x - 1$, each pair of $f$ and $g$ applied in succession will subtract $1$ from the argument. Therefore, applying this 8 times will subtract $8$ from the initial value of $12$.
